FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-redox-ioctl-path.patch last among them, so that it builds against relibc's redox-ioctl. It gives the virtio-gpu driver the render side of slice GP3 of FerrionOS's GPU plan, in new files with hooks in upstream's:
- virtio-gpud acknowledges the virgl, blob and context-init features when the device offers them, reads the capsets at start (bounded: 64 capsets, ids up to 63, 64 KiB, 8 versions), and creates and destroys contexts (render.rs). The commands follow Linux's drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c (MIT). It leaves the device's shared memory region unmapped: blobs and the host-visible window come later.
- driver-graphics registers a second name, gpu.<driver>, beside display.<driver> on the same scheme when the adapter has a render device (GraphicsAdapter::render_device). Its root opens render handles, which serve the version (virtio_gpu 0.1.0), get-parameter, get-capset, context-init and GEM close requests with Linux v7.3's checks and errors (render.rs, ioctl/virtgpu.rs), refuse DRM's own and mode-setting requests with EACCES and everything else with EINVAL, and destroy their context when closed. A context's name is cut at its first zero and kept to printable ASCII before the device sees it.

